   $q$Text B uses the time words "Last year," "First," and "By spring." Why is Text B still best described as problem and solution rather than time order?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Its main purpose is to explain a problem and the steps taken to fix it; the time words only help tell that story.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It compares the school before and after, so time order cannot be part of it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"Any text with the word \"First\" in it is always a problem and solution text.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"Its time words show that the events in it happened centuries ago, like the events in Text A.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Its main purpose is to explain a problem and the steps taken to fix it; the time words only help tell that story.$q$, $q$Text B opens with "had a problem" and ends with the result, so the overall structure is problem and solution. A few time words do not change the overall structure; "First" can appear in many kinds of texts.$q$, 'draft', '800ecc9d-567a-5981-a92e-5f746fae9ff4')
