-- Passage rg5-text-structure-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('281cb22a-b55e-52e4-aecb-c9ebfd7d3e72', 'rg5-text-structure-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-text-structure'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Indoor and Beach Volleyball$q$, $q$Text A: Same Ball, Different Game

Indoor volleyball and beach volleyball share the same basic idea. In both games, players hit a ball over a net and try to make it land on the other side. However, the two games differ in many ways. Indoor teams have six players each, while beach teams have only two. Indoor games are played on a hard wooden floor. Beach games, in contrast, are played on deep sand. Finally, an indoor ball is smaller and harder than the soft beach ball.

Text B: Why Sand Changes Everything

Sand makes beach volleyball a tough sport. When a player pushes off to jump, the sand shifts under the player's feet. Because of this, the player cannot jump as high as on a wooden floor. Running is also slower, since each step sinks into the ground. As a result, beach players must guess where the ball will go and start moving early. The wind outside also pushes the soft ball around. So players learn to read the weather as well as the game.$q$, 'draft')
