insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1f6e1f77-3620-5c2a-8b9c-c21b773fddb3', 'rg5-text-structure-p06', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g5-text-structure'), null,
        '3-5', $q$Streetcars and Buses$q$, $q$Text A: The Streetcars of Ridgeport

In 1890, the city of Ridgeport opened its first electric streetcar line. The cars ran on metal tracks down Main Street. Over the next twenty years, new lines reached every corner of the city. Then, in the 1940s, more families began to buy cars. Fewer people rode the streetcars, and the city removed the tracks one line at a time. The last streetcar made its final trip in 1952. Today, a single restored car sits in the Ridgeport history museum.

Text B: Unsticking Ridgeport's Buses

Ridgeport's buses had a problem. They were stuck in the same traffic jams as everyone else, so riders were often late. Many people gave up and drove instead, which made traffic even worse. To fix this, the city painted red lanes on busy streets that only buses could use. It also gave buses a special signal to turn traffic lights green. Within a year, buses on Main Street were running ten minutes faster. More riders came back.$q$, 'draft')
