   $q$How do the spider and the grasshopper respond differently to the spider's problem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Both of them work together to build a stronger web on the high branch.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"adds-false-detail"},{"text":"The spider wants to quit, but the grasshopper tells her to keep trying.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-characters"},{"text":"Both of them decide that the wind is too strong to fight against.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The grasshopper tells her to quit, but the spider looks for a better solution.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The grasshopper tells her to quit, but the spider looks for a better solution.$q$, $q$The grasshopper says, "Why not give up," while the spider climbs down and studies the wind. The choice "The spider wants to quit, but the grasshopper tells her to keep trying" swaps the two characters' attitudes.$q$, 'draft', '10129b83-73e0-5e8b-80f8-384b42794b81')
