   $q$Which statement best expresses the theme of the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Children are better than adults at noticing small details.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Snowy owls are very rare birds that live in pine trees.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"topic-not-theme"},{"text":"Volunteers should count birds only in the winter months.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"Telling the truth matters, even when it is hard or disappointing.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Telling the truth matters, even when it is hard or disappointing.$q$, $q$Nadia speaks up about the snow even though her cheeks feel hot and the room wants an owl, and she is respected for it. The story never claims children notice more than adults in general.$q$, 'draft', '33545167-b92b-5b90-9991-d84dc4cb5d6f')
