   $q$The Greek root photo means "light," and graph means "write or record." What did the students make when they took a "photograph" of the sky?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A light that shines on the clouds at night","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-graph-root"},{"text":"A written list of the daily weather numbers","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-literal-graph"},{"text":"A picture recorded with light by a camera","is_correct":true},{"text":"A drawing of the sky made with colored pencils","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-photo-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A picture recorded with light by a camera$q$, $q$A photograph is a record made with light, which is what a camera picture is, and the passage later calls them "photos." The written list was the chart, a separate task that uses only the idea of writing.$q$, 'draft', '9adee0c5-4154-5699-a8ec-028bf818610b')
