   $q$The Latin prefix contra- means "against," and dict means "say." What does it show that Mr. Delgado "did not contradict" the boy?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He did not argue that the boy was wrong","is_correct":true},{"text":"He did not let the boy finish speaking","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-interrupt"},{"text":"He did not write the boy's idea down","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-graph-root"},{"text":"He did not hear what the boy had said","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-aud-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He did not argue that the boy was wrong$q$, $q$To contradict is to say something against another person's idea, and instead of arguing, Mr. Delgado agreed it was a good point. He clearly heard the boy, since he answered him, so "He did not hear what the boy had said" does not fit.$q$, 'draft', 'd809b07f-e0a6-5872-8ee0-dbdba5f9beb3')
