   $q$The Greek root bio means "life," and -logist means "one who studies." What does a "biologist" study?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Lenses and how to make them larger","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"The weather and how storms form","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-root-clues"},{"text":"Living things, such as tiny pond creatures","is_correct":true},{"text":"Rocks and the layers of the earth","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-geo-root"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Living things, such as tiny pond creatures$q$, $q$Bio means "life," and the passage defines a biologist as "a scientist who studies living things." Rocks and earth layers are studied by a geologist, which uses the root geo.$q$, 'draft', '424a7571-d6d7-562f-ad2e-e8ae4ed77705')
