   $q$The prefix in- can mean "not," vis means "see," and -ible means "able to be." What does it mean that the creatures are "invisible" to the human eye?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They cannot be seen without help","is_correct":true},{"text":"They can easily be seen by anyone","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-prefix"},{"text":"They hide under rocks in the pond","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They are not able to see people","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-subject"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They cannot be seen without help$q$, $q$Invisible means "not able to be seen," which is why scientists need a microscope. The choice "They are not able to see people" flips the meaning: the creatures cannot be seen, not the other way around.$q$, 'draft', '424a7571-d6d7-562f-ad2e-e8ae4ed77705')
