   $q$Why does the author say that the rocks carried by a glacier "act like sandpaper"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"To explain why people once used glacier rocks to smooth their tools.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To show that glaciers are made of rough sand instead of smooth ice.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"To suggest that glaciers move faster when they carry many rocks along.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"To help readers picture how the rocks scrape and wear down the ground.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$To help readers picture how the rocks scrape and wear down the ground.$q$, $q$The comparison follows the sentence about the glacier dragging rocks along, and it is completed by "scraping the ground," so it helps readers imagine the wearing action. It is not a literal claim that glaciers are made of sand.$q$, 'draft', '78dae235-b4aa-589d-adfe-8e66f54dd7a7')
