   $q$What is the author's point of view about messy sketchbooks?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They are embarrassing, so students should keep them hidden from others.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-opposing-view"},{"text":"They are valuable because they show and support an artist's learning.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They are fine for beginners, but real artists should never keep them.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-detail"},{"text":"They are less useful than sketchbooks filled with only perfect drawings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-position"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They are valuable because they show and support an artist's learning.$q$, $q$The author says, "I want to make a case for the messy sketchbook," and explains how mistakes record learning. Hiding sketchbooks is what some students do, not what the author recommends, and the author says professional artists keep rough pages too.$q$, 'draft', '86ddb0ce-77a6-5278-ae87-3764d4d439a1')
