  ('43b15dac-7501-5bf3-8b92-05717982c3f7', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-authors-purpose'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The author uses phrases such as "Some studies suggest" and "One possible reason." What do these phrases show about the author's approach?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author does not believe any of the studies and wants readers to ignore them all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-purpose"},{"text":"The author is careful not to overstate the evidence, which fits a fair, balanced view.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author is unsure what the passage is about and keeps changing the main topic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"},{"text":"The author is trying to hide that paper is clearly better than screens in every case.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author is careful not to overstate the evidence, which fits a fair, balanced view.$q$, $q$Cautious words like "suggest" and "possible" present findings honestly without claiming more than is known, which matches the even tone. The author still uses the studies as information, so the author is not rejecting them.$q$, 'draft', 'b88db7c0-80f6-59a6-b769-ab4b78cfad92')
