-- Passage rg6-character-setting-plot-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('f550228d-cadc-5fbe-a4fa-c02d3da6697e', 'rg6-character-setting-plot-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Goat and the Upper Path$q$, $q$On a rocky mountain lived a young goat named Brisk, the fastest climber in her herd. Every morning she raced the others to the high ledge, where the sweetest clover grew. Every morning she won.

One spring day an old marmot called to her from his burrow. "Little goat, the ice is melting on the upper path, and the stones there are loose. Take the long trail today."

Brisk laughed. "The long trail is for slow feet." She sprang up the upper path as always.

Halfway up, a stone slid beneath her hoof. She did not fall, but her leg twisted, and she had to limp back down. For a week she could not climb at all. From the meadow she watched the others take the long trail to the ledge, and every evening they came back full and content.

When her leg healed, Brisk found the marmot sunning himself on a flat rock. "You were right," she said. "But why did you warn me when I never once stopped to talk to you?"

"Because I have watched this mountain for many seasons," said the marmot. "It changes with the weather, and so should the way we climb it."

From that day on, Brisk stopped at the marmot's rock each morning before choosing her path. Some days he nodded, and she raced up the upper path. Other days he shook his head, and she took the long trail. She did not always arrive first, but she always arrived.$q$, 'draft')
