  ('b221705d-6c7a-5dc1-9f07-ff580cd1bff0', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-character-setting-plot'), null, 'hard',
   $q$What does Mrs. Pruitt's decision at the end of the story suggest about how the events have changed her view of Opal?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She is mainly pleased that her pies did well at the county fair.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-detail"},{"text":"She is worried Opal will make more mistakes and wants to watch her closely.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"After reading the slips, she trusts Opal to handle the board on her own.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She plans to stop working so that Opal can run the board every day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After reading the slips, she trusts Opal to handle the board on her own.$q$, $q$Mrs. Pruitt reads every slip and then asks Opal to take the board every Saturday, showing new trust. She asks for Saturdays only, not every day, so the choice "She plans to stop working so that Opal can run the board every day" goes beyond the text.$q$, 'draft', 'c43be36e-ca27-5185-ae5f-c332705ab248')
