   $q$How does the relationship between the speaker and Mrs. Lindgren change over the course of the poem?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It changes only because Dad makes the speaker visit her.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It moves from friendship to a quarrel about the tulips.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reversed-sequence"},{"text":"It stays the same, since she still will not wave or talk.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"It moves from avoidance and annoyance to friendly visits.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It moves from avoidance and annoyance to friendly visits.$q$, $q$The speaker begins hoping to avoid her and ends by shoveling her walk first and knocking "just to say hello." The tulip complaint happened before the poem begins, so the relationship does not move toward a quarrel.$q$, 'draft', '105596cb-e9f8-55fb-981b-4c2668ff2b0b')
