   $q$Which sentence best describes how Jonah changes during the story?$q$, $q$[{"text":"He goes from enjoying the podcast to deciding it is too much work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-response"},{"text":"He goes from shy interviewer to the most popular student at school.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"He goes from wanting to give up to finding a fix and planning ahead.","is_correct":true},{"text":"He goes from trusting Mei to doing every task without her.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$He goes from wanting to give up to finding a fix and planning ahead.$q$, $q$Jonah first says "We have to cancel," but then proposes a new episode and later sets up backups. The text never says he becomes the most popular student, which overstates the laughter in Room 14.$q$, 'draft', '0dc46a03-26a8-5261-8bb1-e61ef12493e5')
