insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('0ab7599f-4f90-5ab5-95ef-1f9ce215da73', 'rg6-comparing-texts-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-comparing-texts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Deep End$q$, $q$Text 1: Ten Feet (a story)

Adaeze could swim the whole length of the pool, but only in the shallow lane. Every Saturday, the rest of her swim class lined up at the diving board while she stayed near the wall.

"The water holds you up the same at ten feet as it does at four," said Coach Bello. "The only difference is what you think about it."

Adaeze stood at the edge of the deep end for a long time. She could see the black line on the bottom, far below. Her stomach felt tight. She counted to three twice and did not move.

On the third count, she jumped. The water closed over her head, cold and loud. Then she kicked, and her face broke the surface. She was floating, just as she always did in the shallow lane.

She swam to the ladder, climbed out, and got back in line.

Text 2: At the Edge (a poem)

My toes curl over the tile.
The water is blue and wide.
I can hear my heart.
It is louder than the whistle.

Everyone says it is easy.
Everyone says, just go.
But they are not standing here
with all this blue below.

I breathe in once.
I breathe in twice.
The edge is only an edge.
I bend my knees.$q$, 'draft')
