-- Passage rg6-comparing-texts-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('10bd7318-b812-5f37-a88a-8faa48966d1f', 'rg6-comparing-texts-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-comparing-texts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Long Flight$q$, $q$Text 1: The Tag (a story)

On a bright September morning, Tomas and his grandmother walked through a field of purple flowers with a soft net. Grandma Lupe volunteered with a group that tracked monarch butterflies.

Tomas caught one on his second try. Grandma showed him how to hold it gently by the wings and press a tiny round sticker onto its back wing. The sticker had a number printed on it.

"If someone finds this butterfly in Mexico, they will report the number," Grandma said. "Then we will know how far it went."

Tomas looked at the butterfly. It weighed less than a paper clip. "How does it know where to go?" he asked. "It has never been there."

"Nobody has completely figured that out," Grandma said. "That is one of the best parts."

Tomas opened his fingers. The butterfly drifted up, circled once, and flew south over the trees.

Text 2: Monarch (a poem)

I have never seen the mountains.
I have never seen the pines.
No one drew a map for me
with arrows and with lines.

But something in my orange wings
is pointing me to go.
I cross the rivers and the roads.
I follow what I know.

I am lighter than a paper clip.
The sky is very wide.
I carry the whole long way south
folded up inside.$q$, 'draft')
