   $q$Which theme do both texts share?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Helping others is only worth it when you are thanked.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-meaning"},{"text":"People should stay inside and wait until the snow melts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Neighbors helping one another can make a hard time better.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Winter storms are dangerous and should be feared by all.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Neighbors helping one another can make a hard time better.$q$, $q$Hana and her father clear Mrs. Lindqvist's walk, and the whole lane digs out together and frees a stuck car. In Text 1 the helpers choose not to be thanked, so the choice "Helping others is only worth it when you are thanked" reverses the story's idea.$q$, 'draft', '283a7be9-f4eb-57f6-acbd-625161abbe07')
