   $q$Hana's father says Mrs. Lindqvist's face "is the whole reward." Which part of Text 2 shows a different kind of reward for helping?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The snow falling on each house on the lane during the storm.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"The neighbors cheering together when the stuck car finally rolls free.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The twins handing mittens along the line of people shoveling.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-action-with-reward"},{"text":"Ms. Chen bringing extra salt to sprinkle on the slippery street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-action-with-reward"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The neighbors cheering together when the stuck car finally rolls free.$q$, $q$In Text 2 the reward is the shared joy of success, shown when "We cheer as loud as any crowd," while in Text 1 it is quietly watching one person's happiness. Bringing salt and passing mittens are acts of helping, not the reward that follows.$q$, 'draft', '283a7be9-f4eb-57f6-acbd-625161abbe07')
