   $q$How do the two texts approach the theme of wonder in the night sky differently?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Text 1 finds wonder in a sudden view of a huge sky, while Text 2 finds it in a few stars known well.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Text 1 finds wonder in a few familiar stars, while Text 2 finds it in a sudden view of the galaxy.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-texts"},{"text":"Neither text shows any wonder, since both characters are unhappy with the sky they see.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Text 1 says wonder is only possible in the country, while Text 2 says the same thing about the city.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Text 1 finds wonder in a sudden view of a huge sky, while Text 2 finds it in a few stars known well.$q$, $q$Amira gasps at a sky "crowded with stars" on one night, while the poem's speaker waits for three stars "each night" and knows their names. The speaker still finds wonder in the city, so Text 2 does not reject the city sky.$q$, 'draft', 'dbe62968-0873-5568-b7bd-a826d37e3034')
