   $q$In paragraph 1, the word "arid" means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"covered in tall sand hills","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"located far from any town","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"getting very hot sunshine","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"},{"text":"getting very little rain","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$getting very little rain$q$, $q$The sentence defines the word right after it: arid land "receives less than ten inches of rain in a year." Deserts are often hot, but the text explains "arid" in terms of rain, not heat.$q$, 'draft', '86e3169b-1b47-55bb-a696-cd1f8a911efd')
