   $q$In paragraph 3, what does it mean that dunes "migrate" across the desert?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They change color as the seasons pass.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"},{"text":"They disappear completely in strong winds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They move from one place to another over time.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They grow taller each year in the same spot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They move from one place to another over time.$q$, $q$The paragraph says dunes "do not stay in one spot" and are "moving a few feet or even many yards each year," so migrate means move from place to place. Growing in the same spot is the opposite of what the text describes.$q$, 'draft', '86e3169b-1b47-55bb-a696-cd1f8a911efd')
