   $q$In paragraph 5, the roots of plants "stabilize" the sand. What does "stabilize" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"hold firmly in place","is_correct":true},{"text":"loosen and break up","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"push slowly forward","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"soak with water","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$hold firmly in place$q$, $q$The roots "grip the sand," and as a result "the wind can no longer carry it away," so stabilize means hold steady. Pushing forward is what the wind does to unprotected dunes, the opposite of the roots' job.$q$, 'draft', '86e3169b-1b47-55bb-a696-cd1f8a911efd')
