   $q$In paragraph 2, the frog "stays dormant." What does "dormant" mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"hidden so that predators cannot see","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"inactive for a time, but still alive","is_correct":true},{"text":"no longer alive and never waking","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"hungry after a long period of rest","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$inactive for a time, but still alive$q$, $q$The frog shows "no signs of life" for "weeks at a time," yet paragraph 4 says its heart beats again in spring, so dormant means inactive but alive. The frog is not dead, because it recovers.$q$, 'draft', '25a2c19d-abb7-5486-a0ac-7d3e712c08fb')
