   $q$The author says the method still works because it needs "little more than seawater, sunshine and patience." Which pair of details best supports this claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Some salt is sold for cooking, and much more is used on icy winter roads.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"},{"text":"Algae turn the ponds pink, and visitors mistake them for paint spills.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"The sun evaporates the water, and workers wait months and watch for dry weather.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Workers wash the finished salt, and then they sort the crystals by size.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The sun evaporates the water, and workers wait months and watch for dry weather.$q$, $q$The sun doing the evaporating and the long wait for months and dry weather match "sunshine and patience." The uses of salt are true details, but they describe what happens after the method, not what the method needs.$q$, 'draft', 'f472f129-e4eb-5ce8-af7a-00ea7c98fa7f')
