   $q$Which inference about the end of the ice harvest is best supported by the text?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The ice trade had always been too small to earn much money.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Northern lakes stopped freezing thick enough for crews to cut.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"New machines and refrigerators made lake ice much less needed.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Families decided that they no longer wanted to keep food cold.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$New machines and refrigerators made lake ice much less needed.$q$, $q$The last paragraph names ice-making machines and electric refrigerators just before saying the harvests "mostly disappeared." The trade was not small: the text calls it "a large business" that shipped ice to far ports.$q$, 'draft', '99647ec2-d178-53a7-96fa-253da26efcc8')
