  ('324d1319-8eac-5905-ac20-f63450362579', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g6-evidence-inference'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Haddad warns that a guessed number can "mislead everyone who uses the data." Which detail from the passage best supports this warning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Farmers check the records to decide when to water their fields.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Volunteers read the gauge at about the same time every morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"A rain gauge is a clear tube marked with lines like a measuring cup.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"},{"text":"Haddad trains new volunteers at the public library twice a year.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-supporting-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Farmers check the records to decide when to water their fields.$q$, $q$If farmers make watering choices from the records, a guessed number could lead them to the wrong choice. The detail about training volunteers shows Haddad's work, but not how a wrong number could cause harm.$q$, 'draft', '22b09c01-f556-557b-bf69-21e50aea471a')
